sn35.95:24.1 | S: There’s no desire for sights | T: Not impassioned with forms
sn35.95:24.2 | S: when you see a sight with mindfulness. | T: —seeing a form with mindfulness firm—
sn35.95:24.3 | S: Experiencing it with a mind free of desire, | T: dispassioned in mind, one knows
sn35.95:24.4 | S: you don’t keep clinging to it. | T: and doesn’t remain fastened on it.
sn35.95:25.1 | S: Even as you see a sight | T: While one is seeing a form
sn35.95:25.2 | S: and get familiar with how it feels, | T: —and even experiencing feeling—
sn35.95:25.3 | S: you wear away, you don’t heap up: | T: it falls away and doesn’t accumulate.
sn35.95:25.4 | S: that’s how to live mindfully. | T: Thus one fares mindfully.
